From: Andrzej Rogozynski <sellen@cs-lab.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] client: local games without network support

A local game is run as a fake server plus the client, and the client
learns about the game (balls, shots, score, lost balls, level end) in
comm_recv(), which copies local_game into game via comm_recv_local().
That copy and the handle_mods() it calls are under NETWORK_ENABLED,
and so is the GT_LOCAL check in comm_recv().  Built with
--disable-network the client therefore never sees the server: a fired
ball keeps being drawn on the paddle while the real one flies, is lost
unseen, and the level never goes on.

Take the local path out of the NETWORK_ENABLED guards; only the
packet parser and the network receive loop stay behind them.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Andrzej Rogozynski <sellen@cs-lab.eu>
---
--- a/client/comm.c
+++ b/client/comm.c
@@ -63,7 +63,6 @@
  * game and clear these entries. the current game entry must've
  * been set to 'game'. Ball and shot updates have already been
  * applied to the game context. */
-#ifdef NETWORK_ENABLED
 static void handle_mods()
 {
 	BrickHit *brickhits;
@@ -118,9 +117,6 @@
 	
 	game_reset_mods();
 }
-#endif
-
-#ifdef NETWORK_ENABLED
 /* copy stuff from local_game to game */
 static void comm_recv_local( void )
 {
@@ -183,6 +179,7 @@
 	return;
 }
 
+#ifdef NETWORK_ENABLED
 /* parse incoming packets and handle them according to the client's
  * state */
 static void comm_parse_packet()
@@ -420,14 +417,13 @@
  * in the current state. */
 void comm_recv( void )
 {
-#ifdef NETWORK_ENABLED
-	int recv_limit;
-	
 	/* fake communication in local game */
 	if ( game->game_type == GT_LOCAL ) {
 		comm_recv_local();
 		return;
 	}
+#ifdef NETWORK_ENABLED
+	int recv_limit;
 	
 	if ( !client_is_connected ) return;
 
